{
  "_doc": "L4 texture layer (docs/textures.md). A slot says how a set in content/textures/<set>/ is sampled: mode detail = multiplies the procedural pattern (structure, per-stone tint, finishes stay), replace = the set's own structure instead of the pattern; space asset = triplanar in asset space, part = the part's dominant face with v along its grain axis, world = triplanar in world space, ground = planar xz. albedo / normal / rough / ao = strengths 0..1 (albedo and roughness are taken relative to the set's mean, so the material colour stays). height = metres fed into the derivative bump. scale multiplies the set's tile frequency. rot = quarter turns. fade = [start, end] m from the eye. patterns: pattern id -> slot; materials: material name -> slot (\"none\" = procedural only), checked before the pattern; a material's own \"texture\" field wins over both. terrain: the kTerrainFS layers.",
